text:
I've applied both of your decisions and the review's fixes.

- **Project id:** a stable `project:` id goes in `rpir/config.yaml`. It defaults to the folder name and never changes when you rename the folder. The importer takes `--project-id`, so old retros cited under `project A` count towards the same project.
- **Retro re-run:** re-recording a change first removes that change's earlier occurrences, then records the new set.
- **Technical fixes:**
  - every audit entry records the size judged, skipped findings included;
  - regression is checked against the newest shipped version;
  - each occurrence has its own finding id field;
  - the no-node behaviour is owned by M3 (nudge) and M6 (retro step, improve skills);
  - audit file names come from the full repo path, so two repos with the same folder name can't collide;
  - the version test accepts any version from 0.7.0 up, so the next patch bump won't break it;
  - M2 may touch the hook files it needs for the failing nav tests;
  - migration removes project A's `docs/changes` → `rpir/changes` symlinks instead of copying through them.

The plan validates. Its only warnings are the two known false positives from M1 working in `../milestoned-plan-dag`.

A second diff review is checking these edits in the background. If it comes back clean, you approve and I commit.
